course: dictionary
lesson: 9797
title: Suspicious: when something does not feel right
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Suspicious is an adjective, and it has two main meanings. The first is about something that looks wrong, dangerous or dishonest, like «a suspicious package». The second is about not trusting someone or something, like «The cat was suspicious of the new dog.»
explain: Use the words around it to work out which meaning fits. In «Bro, that line judge is sus!», the word sus is short slang for suspicious, so the judge seems unfair or dodgy. Ask: what word would fit here? Then put suspicious in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Suspicious often describes a feeling of warning. You can feel suspicious before you know for sure that something is wrong, and that feeling is a clue to tell an adult.
fact: Suspicious means making you think something is wrong, dangerous or dishonest.
fact: Suspicious can also mean not trusting someone or something.
fact: If you see a suspicious package, do not touch it, and tell an adult straight away.
fact: «Sus» is young slang for suspicious, and «dodgy» is another word people use with the same meaning.
fact: You can say suspicious of someone, or talk about suspicious behaviour.
exercise: «The cat was suspicious of the new dog.» What does suspicious mean here? | *Not trusting the new dog | Hungry for dinner | Very happy to see the dog | Fast asleep next to the dog
exercise: In a safety lesson, what should you do with a suspicious package? | *Do not touch it, and tell an adult | Give it to a friend to hold | Open it quickly to see what is inside | Take it home to keep it safe
exercise: Mason yelled «Bro, that line judge is sus!» What does sus mean here? | *Dodgy, or suspicious | Fast in a race | Happy and friendly | Very tall
test: An email asks you to click a link to win a prize, and you do not know who sent it. Why might it be suspicious? | It is written in red, so it must be true | It is definitely a real prize, so click it now | Clicking is the safest way to check | *It may be a scam, so do not click it
test: In a detective story, the detective notices suspicious behaviour. What does suspicious behaviour mean? | Behaviour that is dancing in a circle | Behaviour that is quiet and sleepy | *Behaviour that seems wrong or dishonest | Behaviour that is very kind and helpful
exam: Which sentence shows someone is not trusting something? | The sun was shining brightly over the park | Dad made pancakes for breakfast on Sunday | The dog wagged its tail at the stranger | *Ella was suspicious of the stranger's offer
